    "result_text": "The full test suite is the single `AcceptanceTest` class, and all tests pass with a clean `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the optional owner `email` field per the spec: present-and-valid \u2192 stored/returned lower-cased; present-but-invalid \u2192 400; absent \u2192 accepted.\n\nChanges, following the repo's existing telephone-normalization pattern:\n\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added an optional `email` string property to the `OwnerFields` schema, so the generated `OwnerFieldsDto`/`OwnerDto` (and MapStruct `OwnerMapper`) carry it automatically.\n- **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added the `email` column with getter/setter.\n- **`function/owner/BuildOwner.java`** (POST pipeline) \u2014 when `email` is present, validate it syntactically (`^[^@\\s]+@[^@\\s]+\\.[^@\\s]+$`), lower-case it, and store it; blank/absent \u2192 `null`; invalid \u2192 throws the checked `InvalidEmailException`.\n- **`function/owner/ApplyOwner.java`** (PUT pipeline) \u2014 carries the email through, lower-cased.\n- **`escalation/InvalidEmailException.java`** + **`InvalidEmailExceptionHandler.java`** + **`officefloor/escalation/...InvalidEmailException.yml`** \u2014 maps the exception to a 400 `ProblemDetail`, mirroring `InvalidTelephoneException`.\n- **DB schemas** (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `mysql`, `postgres`) \u2014 added the nullable `email` column. Also converted the positional `INSERT INTO owners VALUES (...)` seed rows in `hsqldb`/`mysql` to named-column inserts so the extra column doesn't break the seed data (`h2`/`postgres` already named columns).\n\nThe three new acceptance tests (`coreLowercasesEmail`, `errorRejectsInvalidEmail`, `functionalityAcceptsMissingEmail`) and the full suite pass.",
